      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>PoPuLA B. CONCERT, BOLD STREET SCHOOL-ROOM TO-NIGHT AT 7.30. SPECIAL ATTRACTION. MR. BERT HOLLINGWORTH'S "COMEDY COURTIERS." A NIGHT OF REFINED HUMOUR. Admission 1 penny. Gallery 2 pence. CITY EXHIBITION ALL, LIVERPOOL RD., DEANSGATE. Manchester. THE GREAT BOSTOCK ARENA AND JUNGLE, The World's Greatest Trainers Present Earth's Most Marvellous Trained LIONS, TIGERS, ELEPHANTS. JAGUARS, BEARS, &amp;c., IN LARGEST STEEL CAGE EVER BUILT. • THE JUNGLE OPENS DAILY AT 2 &amp; 7. ARENIC PERFORMANCES COMMENCE 2.50 &amp; 7.50. ADMISSION ONE SHILLING. CHILDREN 6d.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON ARTS AND CRAFTS SOCIETY. THIRD ANNUAL EXHIBITION, AT TRINITY CHAMBERS, MARKET GATE, WAI:RINGTON. DECEMBER 14TH TO 18TH INCL USIVE. OPENING By MRS. A. H. CROSFIELIT ON TUESDAY, DECEMBER 14TH, AT 3 P.M. A. HAYWARD, Hon. Sec.</p>
