      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <p>WARRINGTON WOMEN'S CIRCLE.— SUNDAY, DEC. STII AT 3 O'CLOCK. MRS. LETHEREN. SOLOIST: MISS MAY ISHERWOOD. WEDNESDAY AT 8 P.m.—A MEETING WITH LANTERN FOR MISS WESTON'S WORK AMONG THE SAILORS. CHAIR: ALDERMAN BENNETT. FANCY WORK WILL BE ON SALE FOR CHRISTMAS GIFTS. NO ADMISSION. OFFERING. FRIDAY AT 7.30 P.M.-LESSON IN PAPER DECORATIONS, MISS GORNALL. TUESDAY AT 3 p.m.—B.W.T.A. MEETING. "The grace of Cheerfulness," IRS. GLADDING.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>CIOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— The HEALTH COMMITTEE hereby invite TENDERS for the supply of the undermentioned goods, to bqi used in the Corporation Hospitals dttring the six months ending June 30tb, 1910. GROCERIES, PROVISIONS, CLEANING MATERIALS, BREAD AND FLOUR, MILK, FISH, GAME AND POULTRY, MEAT.</p>
        <p>Full particulars and forms (on which alone tender are to be made) to be obtained at the Health Depart meat Office, Sankey St. The forms to be put in envelopes, sealed and endorsed "Tenders for Provisions," and addressed to the "Chair- man of the Health Committee." No tender will he considered that arrives at the above-mentioned office after 12 noon on Tuesday. the 14th December. The greatest stringency will be observed in maintain- ing the rules laid down. J. COCiTE HIBBERT, Medical Superintendent of Corporation Hospitals.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. -- TO BUILDERS AND CONTRACTORS. __</p>
        <p>The TOWN HALL, PARK and BATHS COMMITTEE of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive Tenders for the Erection and Completion of 2 New Swimming Baths, New Slipper Baths and Sundry Alterations to the Corporation Baths. Drawings, specifications, Btc., may be seen, and forms of tender bills of quhntities, and all further informa- tion obtained at the Office of the BoroughSurveyor,Town Hall, on and after Friday, the 10th day of December, at which place tenders must be delivered on or before 12 o'clock on Thursday, the 30th day of December, 1909. A deposit of 22 2s. will be required for quantities which sum will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Cheques to ~be made payable to the Borough Treasurer, Warrington. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. THOS. LON GDIN, Borough Engineer and Surveyor. Bor.iugh Engineer and Surveyor's Office, December 3rd, 1909.</p>
      </div>
