        <p>Warrington Albions Res. have withdrawn. Matches for Saturday 4th December. Well field v Newton Amateurs. Warrington "Observer" Cup.—Second Round. Clock Face v. Orford Albion. Bethell Mission v. Prescot Wesley. Warrington Albions v. Whitecross. Widnes Town v. Prescot Athletic. To be played on December 11th.</p>
        <p>_ _ Results for November 25th. Newton Amateurs 3, Howley Athletic 3. Earlestown St. John's, 2 ; Whitecross 1.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON ALBIoNS v. WIDNES TOWN.—Warring- ton Albions visited Widnes last Saturday and played Widnes Town. The visiting team had to play up hill but they pressed forward and had several attempts at goal. Only once were Widnes likely to get a goal, but Makin for the Albions with a splendid effort managed to keep them out. There was no score on either side when the half time whistle blew. Resuming the visit- ing team again pressed and were having it all their own way until about 15 minutes off time. Widnes broke away and sent in a fine shot. This was the first goal of the match and no more being secured the result was: Widnes Town, 1 ; Warrington Albions, nil.</p>
        <p>To-day (Saturday) Warrington Albions play Sutton Commercial at Liverpool-road. Warrington Albion's team : Goal, Makin; full backs, Sergeant and Short ; half backs, Dilworth, Dickenson and E. Whitfield ; forwards, Ritchie, Thomas, T. Whitfield, Taylor and Cheaters.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>FRIENDLY MATCH.</head>
        <p>FRIENDLY MATCH.</p>
        <p>MOORE V. ASTON HALL.-Th is match was played a Moore on Saturday in wet weather. At the interval noither side had scored. On re-starting E. Clarke scored with a low shot, giving Basnett no chance. At the other end Dean put in a fast drive, which Londan dealt with in masterly fashion. With ten minutes to go, F. Roscoe, receiving a pass from Hughes, scored a second goal for Moore. F. Wilkman and Cartwright defended well for the winners. Final result : Moore. two goals ; Aston, nil.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
