      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-04_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>KAISER'S SON AND THE GERMAN NAVY.</head>
        <p>KAISER'S SON AND THE GERMAN NAVY.</p>
        <p>The • Kaiser's second son, Prince Eitel Friedrich, whose photograph is given herewith, is a firm believer in the German Imperial idea and its embodiment in the German Navy. Speaking at the banquet in connection with the launch of the German Dreadnought " Thuringen " hi dwelt on the unceasing labours of all connected with the Fleet to bring it to the "highest point of readiness for war." His Imperial Highness went on to say that "everyone whose privilege it has been to fall in with a German ship in foreign waters knows what pleasure it is to sight a ship flying the imperial red, white, and black. How the heart bounds when the cherished war ensign greets one from the masthead!" and so on. Altogether the young Prince made a remarkable speech, and there is no doubt whatever that the Kaiser's second son is "a chip of the old block."</p>
