        <p>THE FINANCIAL SIDE OF AVIATION. There is money in being able to fly. M. Louis Paulhan has provisionally agreed to go to America and perform a series of flights throughout the Continent for a period of six months at a salary of £4,000 a month. In addition, all his expenses will be paid, and his two assistants are to be engaged independently, so that M. Paulhan stands to pocket ,E 24,000 by the trip. Of late, large sums have been paid to aviators, but this offer is unprecedented. M. Pauthan is expected to start his flight in California early in January.</p>
